Rock Classification Scheme — British Geological Survey (@mp-classification: 0, is #reference, #part-of @mp-sources) { r_0715XKKA34SBMSRTCCZD3KJQEH
British Geological Survey authors. [Official Rock Classification Scheme, explanatory reports, search, and downloads](https://www.bgs.ac.uk/technologies/bgs-rock-classification-scheme/).

Read the complete igneous, metamorphic, and sediment/sedimentary-rock reports as their topics arise, preserving each report's authors, date, edition, and purpose. The official page explains relationships with IUGS and the scheme's deliberate refinements; BGS and IUGS names are not automatically interchangeable. Separate descriptive naming criteria from an interpretation of origin or tectonic environment.

The official page supplies freely downloadable reports and a maintained classification. Preserve actual UKRI/BGS and component terms rather than assuming all reports or every linked product share one open licence. Status, report categories, principles, and authorized source routes checked on 29 October 2026. No nomenclature database or report collection is mirrored.

